# Academic Achievements — Experimental Aerodynamics

This section presents research carried out at **Politecnico di Milano** on spoileron effectiveness for a low-aspect-ratio swept wing with reflex airfoils, connected to a wider aircraft-design and control-surface development activity.

The work was published at **IOCAE 2026** and received the **Best Poster Award**.

## My Contribution

As a co-author, my work included:

- wind-tunnel test planning and execution;
- aerodynamic data processing and reduction;
- comparison between experimental and analytical predictions;
- assessment of rolling effectiveness and yaw coupling;
- interpretation of results for control-surface sizing and aircraft design.

The activity gave me direct experience in the full experimental loop from **test definition to validated engineering decision**.
